msgid "Update"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"It is with great pleasure that we are announcing the release of Quarkus 3.6."
"0."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Quarkus 3.6 will be the last minor of the year (we will release micros for 3."
"6 in December though).\n"
"Quarkus 3.7 is https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/wiki/Release-"
"Planning[planned for the end of January]."
msgstr ""

msgid "Major changes are:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Several new features in the REST Client related to SSE handling"
msgstr ""

msgid "Many OIDC and general security enhancements (see below for details)"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Move `quarkus-jaeger` and `quarkus-smallrye-opentracing` to Quarkiverse"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"As usual, this version also comes with bugfixes, performance improvements "
"and documentation improvements."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"As mentioned in the previous minor announcement, we currently maintain two "
"version streams in the community:"
msgstr ""

msgid "3.6: it is the latest and greatest and it introduces new features"
msgstr ""

msgid "3.2: it is our current link:/blog/lts-releases/[LTS release]"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Quarkus 2.x is not maintained in the community anymore.\n"
"If you are using the community version, please upgrade to Quarkus 3.x "
"(either 3.2 LTS or 3.6)."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"To update to Quarkus 3.6, we recommend updating to the latest version of the "
"Quarkus CLI and run:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"To migrate from 3.5, please refer to https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/"
"wiki/Migration-Guide-3.6[our migration guide]."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If you are not already using 3.x, please refer to the https://quarkus.io/"
"blog/quarkus-3-0-final-released/[3.0 announcement] for all the details.\n"
"You can also refer to https://quarkus.io/blog/quarkus-3-upgrade/[this blog "
"post] for additional details.\n"
"Once you upgraded to 3.0, also have a look at the https://github.com/"
"quarkusio/quarkus/wiki/Migration-Guide-3.1[3.1], https://github.com/"
"quarkusio/quarkus/wiki/Migration-Guide-3.2[3.2], https://github.com/"
"quarkusio/quarkus/wiki/Migration-Guide-3.2[3.3], https://github.com/"
"quarkusio/quarkus/wiki/Migration-Guide-3.4[3.4], and https://github.com/"
"quarkusio/quarkus/wiki/Migration-Guide-3.5[3.5] migration guides."
msgstr ""

msgid "What&#8217;s new?"
msgstr ""

msgid "SSE handling improvements"
msgstr ""

msgid "SSE handling in the REST Client was significantly improved:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The REST Client can now return the entire SSE event instead of just the data."
""
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You can easily filter out some particular SSE events with a `SseEventFilter`."
""
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"These new features are fully documented in the https://quarkus.io/guides/"
"rest-client-reactive[REST Client guide]."
msgstr ""

msgid "OIDC and security improvements"
msgstr ""

msgid "Many enhancements were made to the OIDC and security extensions:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Support for dynamic OIDC JWK set resolution"
msgstr ""

msgid "Ability to adjust HTTP permissions and roles policies at runtime"
msgstr ""

msgid "Add Discord as well-known OIDC provider"
msgstr ""

msgid "JPA Security: allow pointing to a named persistence unit"
msgstr ""

msgid "Introduce OidcRequestFilter"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Make it possible to acquire OIDC SecurityIdentity after HTTP request has "
"completed"
msgstr ""

msgid "Also there is now an OIDC client integration for GraphQL clients."
msgstr ""

msgid "quarkus-jaeger and quarkus-smallrye-opentracing moved to Quarkiverse"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"After having been deprecated for a long while, the Jaeger and SmallRye "
"OpenTracing extensions have been retired from the Quarkus Platform."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"It is recommended to  migrate your applications to OpenTelemetry and a  "
"https://quarkus.io/version/main/guides/telemetry-opentracing-to-otel-"
"tutorial[tutorial to guide you in this migration is available]."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The code of the extensions have been moved to the Quarkiverse and can be "
"consumed from there from now on (relocations have been put in place to avoid "
"breaking your builds).\n"
"If you want these extensions to continue working in the future, it is "
"recommended to get involved in their development."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"These extensions are not in the Quarkus Platform BOM anymore and you need to "
"define the version yourself in your build file, together with moving to the "
"new `groupId`:"
msgstr ""

